WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.173 --> 00:00:16.135
afternoon Anne happily walked home from school.

2
00:00:16.916 --> 00:00:19.178
"What a nice month November has been!"

3
00:00:19.618 --> 00:00:20.098
she said.

4
00:00:20.799 --> 00:00:24.502
Anne had never quite stopped her childhood habit of talking to herself.

5
00:00:25.603 --> 00:00:30.547
When she arrived at Green Gables, she found Marilla in the yard, looking very anxious.

6
00:00:31.368 --> 00:00:33.477
"Anne, Dora is lost!"

7
00:00:33.897 --> 00:00:34.637
cried Marilla.

8
00:00:34.657 --> 00:00:37.018
"Dora! Lost?"

9
00:00:37.958 --> 00:00:41.600
Anne looked at Davy, who was sitting on the yard gate, swinging his feet.

10
00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:44.321
"Davy, do you know where she is?"

11
00:00:44.341 --> 00:00:48.102
"No, I don't," replied Davy.

12
00:00:48.122 --> 00:00:54.945
"When I left at one o'clock," said Marilla, "Dora was playing with her doll in the kitchen, and

13
00:00:55.065 --> 00:00:57.246
Davy was making mud pies in the yard."

14
00:00:57.266 --> 00:01:01.608
"Dora must be somewhere," said Anne.

15
00:01:02.492 --> 00:01:04.394
"She would never wander far by herself.

16
00:01:05.174 --> 00:01:06.996
Perhaps she fell asleep inside."

17
00:01:08.077 --> 00:01:09.278
Marilla shook her head.

18
00:01:09.298 --> 00:01:11.620
"I've looked in every room.

19
00:01:12.961 --> 00:01:14.802
But she might be somewhere nearby."

20
00:01:14.822 --> 00:01:19.366
A thorough search of the yard, the barn, and the orchard followed.

21
00:01:20.187 --> 00:01:23.109
Finally Anne and Marilla met again in the front yard.

22
00:01:23.129 --> 00:01:24.930
"Where can she be?"

23
00:01:25.471 --> 00:01:26.532
said Anne, worried.

24
00:01:27.513 --> 00:01:31.456
"Maybe she tumbled into the well," suggested Davy cheerfully.

25
00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:35.162
Anne and Marilla looked fearfully into each other's eyes.

26
00:01:35.182 --> 00:01:39.124
"She she might have," whispered Marilla.

27
00:01:40.064 --> 00:01:42.866
The Green Gables' well was the deepest in Avonlea.

28
00:01:43.546 --> 00:01:48.849
Feeling faint, Anne ran to the well and peered at the tiny glimmer of water far below.

29
00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:53.472
She lowered a lantern into the well, but she did not see Dora.

30
00:01:54.232 --> 00:01:55.813
Anne breathed a sigh of relief.

31
00:01:57.274 --> 00:01:59.415
"It's all right, Marilla," Anne called.

32
00:01:59.435 --> 00:02:01.416
"Dora didn't fall down the well!"

33
00:02:03.116 --> 00:02:04.758
"Do you think Dora went to Mr.

34
00:02:04.798 --> 00:02:05.738
Harrison's house?"

35
00:02:06.179 --> 00:02:06.979
Marilla asked.

36
00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:10.623
"He's on vacation now, and there's no one there.

37
00:02:11.623 --> 00:02:14.065
Dora is always talking about his parrot."

38
00:02:14.085 --> 00:02:17.148
"I'll go over and see," said Anne.

39
00:02:18.549 --> 00:02:22.753
Just then Davy's smile disappeared and he quietly ran to the barn.

40
00:02:23.794 --> 00:02:25.715
Neither Marilla nor Anne noticed.

41
00:02:27.257 --> 00:02:30.920
Mr. Harrison's house was locked, and the windows were all closed.

42
00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:34.262
Anne stood on the veranda and called Dora loudly.

43
00:02:35.043 --> 00:02:37.484
Ginger the parrot was in his cage in the kitchen.

44
00:02:38.165 --> 00:02:40.326
He shrieked and swore fiercely.

45
00:02:41.547 --> 00:02:46.971
Between the parrot's outbursts Anne heard a small cry from the little wooden shed in the yard.

46
00:02:47.691 --> 00:02:49.933
Anne ran to the shed door and opened it.

47
00:02:50.433 --> 00:02:54.816
She saw Dora, sitting on a wooden box, her face wet with tears.

48
00:02:54.836 --> 00:02:58.079
"Oh, Dora," said Anne.

49
00:02:58.099 --> 00:02:59.900
"We were so worried!

50
00:03:00.372 --> 00:03:01.913
What are you doing in here?"

51
00:03:01.933 --> 00:03:10.858
"Davy and I came over to see Ginger," sobbed Dora, "but we couldn't see Ginger through the window.

52
00:03:10.878 --> 00:03:19.463
Then Davy brought me here," Dora continued, "and he ran out and shut the door, and I couldn't

53
00:03:19.523 --> 00:03:20.124
get out!

54
00:03:21.905 --> 00:03:27.368
Oh, I'm so hungry and cold, and I thought you'd never come, Anne."

55
00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:31.801
"Davy?" Anne said, shocked.

56
00:03:32.761 --> 00:03:35.122
She carried Dora home with a heavy heart.

57
00:03:36.043 --> 00:03:37.603
Davy had lied to her.

58
00:03:39.104 --> 00:03:44.546
Anne had grown to love Davy dearly, and it hurt her to discover that he had deliberately lied.

59
00:03:45.326 --> 00:03:49.208
Once they were home, Anne gave Dora some dinner and put her to bed.

60
00:03:50.088 --> 00:03:55.771
Marilla came grimly into the house with Davy, whom she had found hiding in the darkest corner of

61
00:03:55.811 --> 00:03:56.351
the barn.

62
00:03:57.331 --> 00:04:00.505
Davy looked up at Anne, hopeful that she might forgive him.

63
00:04:00.885 --> 00:04:03.747
But there was no trace of a smile in Anne's eyes.

64
00:04:03.767 --> 00:04:06.448
"How could you do this, Davy?"

65
00:04:06.869 --> 00:04:08.129
Anne asked sorrowfully.

66
00:04:08.149 --> 00:04:11.832
"I just did it for fun," said Davy.

67
00:04:11.852 --> 00:04:16.254
"Things have been so quiet around here, I thought it would be fun to give you and Marilla

68
00:04:16.294 --> 00:04:17.215
a big scare."

69
00:04:17.235 --> 00:04:20.977
"It wasn't fun, Davy," said Anne.

70
00:04:20.997 --> 00:04:22.538
"And you lied."

71
00:04:22.558 --> 00:04:24.659
"Of course I did!"

72
00:04:25.099 --> 00:04:26.956
said Davy.

73
00:04:26.976 --> 00:04:29.437
"If I hadn't lied, you wouldn't have been scared.

74
00:04:30.517 --> 00:04:31.517
I had to lie."

75
00:04:31.537 --> 00:04:34.418
"Oh, Davy, how could you?"

76
00:04:34.918 --> 00:04:35.498
Anne said.

77
00:04:36.059 --> 00:04:37.439
She had tears in her eyes.

78
00:04:37.459 --> 00:04:40.820
"Don't you know how wrong it was?"

79
00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:43.861
Davy was suddenly horrified.

80
00:04:44.681 --> 00:04:46.181
He had made Anne cry.

81
00:04:47.782 --> 00:04:52.443
Marilla left the room, and Davy rushed to Anne and flung his arms around her neck.

82
00:04:52.463 --> 00:04:57.192
"I didn't know it was wrong to tell lies," he sobbed.

83
00:04:57.212 --> 00:04:59.473
"How could I know it was wrong?

84
00:04:59.493 --> 00:05:04.874
Now you'll never love me and I'm sure Paul Irving never tells lies.

85
00:05:06.875 --> 00:05:09.076
I'm trying to be as good as him."

86
00:05:10.816 --> 00:05:16.658
When Davy was convinced that Anne had finally forgiven him, he apologized to Marilla and went to bed.

87
00:05:17.458 --> 00:05:21.439
Later Marilla exclaimed to Anne, "What will we do with him?

88
00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:23.380
He's so naughty!"

89
00:05:24.848 --> 00:05:26.329
"Oh, don't say that, Marilla.

90
00:05:26.830 --> 00:05:29.372
Remember how bad I was when I first came here?"

91
00:05:29.812 --> 00:05:30.653
replied Anne.

92
00:05:32.154 --> 00:05:33.195
Marilla smiled.

93
00:05:33.916 --> 00:05:35.758
Anne, of course, did have a point.
